# One extractor with one work in it, worked twice, and the second time there is nothing left.
#
# **This is the hole the test beside it had.** `work` required an extractor and consumed a labor,
# so an extractor could be worked as often as there was labor for it - Sean, 2026-09-17, reading
# `a-food-extractor-and-a-metal-extractor-do-not-interfere`: *an extractor can be used as many
# times as we have labor for.*
#
# **There is labor for the second one**, which is what makes this about the readiness and not
# about the labor.

{test name:an-extractor-cannot-be-worked-twice-on-one-readiness}

{given}
{territory id:1}
{deposit where:1 what:31 density:6 quantity:1}
{extractor where:1 what:31 working:1 quantity:1}
{labor where:1 quantity:2}

{when}
{work where:1 what:31}
{work where:1 what:31}

{refused}
{extractor where:1 what:31 working:1 quantity:1}
